+/* Machine-code cache. nv50_ir turns the TGSI of every new program into GPU
+ * code, 5-30 ms per stage on the Switch CPU, and glProgramBinary pays that
+ * again because a GL program binary holds only TGSI. The result of translate
+ * for the same tokens goes into Mesa's disk cache (needs MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR),
+ * keyed by the inputs below plus the driver keys (build id of this Mesa).
+ *
+ * Compute programs (symbol tables) and stream output (the tfb state is built
+ * from the codegen info) are not cached.
